# clause-runtime-zig — the runtime proper

Zig-authored dynamic library implementing macro interpretation,
scratch lowering, and generative expansion against Clause IR
buffers received through the C ABI defined by
`clause-runtime-abi`. Delivered as
`libclause_runtime.{so|dylib|dll}` bundled alongside the compiler
binary.

## Building

```sh
cd mock/runtime-zig
zig build
```

Output lands at `zig-out/lib/libclause_runtime.{so|dylib|dll}`
(extension depends on host OS).

## How the Rust side locates the binary

Phase 6 skeleton round does not yet locate the binary; the
Rust-side `RuntimeLoader::load` returns
`LoaderError::NotImplemented`. Follow-up rounds wire a locate
path:

- `CLAUSE_RUNTIME_PATH` environment variable — explicit path
  to the dylib.
- Fallback: next-to-Rust-binary convention.
- Fallback: embedded runtime (statically linked lightweight
  backend, for test / dev use).

See `BACKLOG.md` for the full deferred-feature list.

## Build status

Mockspace does NOT build this tree. The Zig tree ships source
only; `cargo mock check` ignores `.zig` files. Validate the
Zig side by running `zig build` manually or via a CI job.

## Skeleton-round scope

Phase 6 skeleton (2026-04-20) ships three `extern "C"` stubs:

- `clause_runtime_new() ?*anyopaque` → null.
- `clause_runtime_free(?*anyopaque) void` → no-op.
- `clause_runtime_execute(?*anyopaque, [*]const u8, usize) ClauseResult`
  → `{ .code = -1 }`.

Real interpreter body lands in follow-up rounds.
